1
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,700
Okay, if no one else will say it, I will.

2
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:15,050
We really suck at paintball.

3
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:17,050
That was absolutely humiliating.

4
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:20,200
Oh, come on. Some battles you win, some battles you lose.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:25,960
Yes, but you don't have to lose to Kyle Bernstein's bar mitzvah party.

6
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:27,450
I think we have to acknowledge,

7
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:31,870
those were some fairly savage preadolescent Jews.

8
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:36,080
No,we were annihilated by our own incompetence

9
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,150
and the inability of some people to follow the chain of command.

10
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:40,800
Sheldon,let it go!

11
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:45,420
No,I want to talk about the fact that Wolowitz shot me in the back.

12
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:46,970
I shot you for good reason.

13
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:50,230
You were leading us into disaster.

14
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:52,690
I was giving clear,concise orders.

15
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:55,060
You hid behind a tree yelling,"Get the kid in the yarmulke!

16
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:57,250
Get the kid in the yarmulke!"

17
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:58,460
Oh,hey,guys.

18
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:01,400
-Oh,hey,Penny. Hello. -Morning,ma'am.

19
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,770
So,how was paintball?Did you have fun?

20
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:08,130
Sure,if you consider being fragged by your own troops fun.

21
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:12,330
You clear space on your calendar--there will be an inquiry.

22
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:13,650
Okay.

23
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:14,920
Um,hey,I'm having a party on Saturday,

24
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:16,540
so if you guys are around,you should come on by.

25
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:17,750
-A party? -Yeah.

26
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:21,380
A... "boy-girl" party?

27
00:01:22,210 --> 00:01:26,190
Well,there will be boys and there will be girls and it is a party,so...

28
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:27,320
It'll just be a bunch of my friends.

29
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:29,290
We'll have some beer,do a little dancing.

30
00:01:29,290 --> 00:01:30,180
Dancing?

31
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:31,590
Yeah,I don't know,Penny...

32
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:32,560
The thing is,we're not...

33
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,940
-No,we're really more of a... -No.

34
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:38,110
But thanks.Thanks for thinking of us.

35
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:40,230
Are you sure? Come on,it's Halloween.

36
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:41,590
A Halloween party?

37
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:43,180
As in... costumes?

38
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:46,140
Well,yeah.

39
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,940
Is there a theme?

40
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,400
Um,yeah,Halloween.

41
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:00,920
Yes,but are the costumes random,or genre-specific?

42
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,390
As usual,I'm not following.

43
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:07,690
He's asking if we can come as anyone from science fiction,fantasy...

44
00:02:07,690 --> 00:02:09,080
-Sure.  -What about comic books?

45
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,110
-Fine.  -Anime?

46
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:11,440
-Of course.  -TV,film,

47
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:13,860
D- and-D,manga,Greek gods,Roman gods,Norse gods--

48
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:15,890
Anything you want! Okay?

49
00:02:15,890 --> 00:02:19,010
Any costume you want.

50
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:21,340
Bye.

51
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:25,020
Gentlemen,to the sewing machines.

52
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:47,820
The.Middle.Earth.Paradigm

53
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,030
I'll get it.

54
00:03:08,450 --> 00:03:11,090
Oh,no.

55
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:13,730
Oh,no.

56
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:17,390
Make way for the fastest man alive!

57
00:03:17,390 --> 00:03:18,760
Oh,no.

58
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:21,640
See,this is why I wanted to have a costume meeting.

59
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:24,600
We all have other costumes: We can change.

60
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,190
Or we could walk right behind each other all night

61
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:30,810
and look like one person going really fast.

62
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:38,720
No,no,no.

63
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:43,140
It's a boy-girl party,this flash runs solo.

64
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:44,510
Okay,how about this?

65
00:03:44,510 --> 00:03:45,770
Nobody gets to be The Flash.

66
00:03:45,770 --> 00:03:48,490
We all change. Agreed?

67
00:03:48,490 --> 00:03:50,890
Agreed.

68
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,220
I call Frodo!

69
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:55,600
Damn!

70
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:02,670
Hey.

71
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:09,090
Sorry I'm late,but my hammer got stuck in the door on the bus.

72
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:10,430
You went with Thor?

73
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:14,240
What,just because I'm Indian I can't be a Norse god?

74
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:17,400
"No,no,Raj has to be an Indian god."

75
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:18,870
That's racism.

76
00:04:18,870 --> 00:04:20,910
I mean look at Wolowitz.He's not English,

77
00:04:20,910 --> 00:04:23,770
but he's dressed like Peter Pan.

78
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,870
Sheldon is neither sound nor light,

79
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:28,790
but he's obviously the Doppler effect.

80
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,730
I'm not Peter Pan.

81
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:35,510
I'm Robin Hood.

82
00:04:35,510 --> 00:04:36,430
Really?

83
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:40,750
Because I sawPeter Pan,and you're dressed exactly like Cathy Rigby.

84
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:45,210
She was a little bigger than you,but it's basically the same look,man.

85
00:04:46,070 --> 00:04:46,780
Hey,Sheldon

86
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:48,920
There's something I want to talk to you about before we go to the party.

87
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,550
I don't care if anybody gets it.

88
00:04:50,550 --> 00:04:53,230
I'm going as the Doppler effect.

89
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:57,170
-No,it's not that. -If I have to,I can demonstrate.

90
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:03,090
Terrific.

91
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:07,130
this party is my first chance for Penny

92
00:05:07,130 --> 00:05:09,860
to see me in the context of her social group,

93
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:13,140
and I need you not to embarrass me tonight.

94
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,740
Well,what exactly do you mean by embarrass you?

95
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:18,830
Well,for example,tonight,

96
00:05:18,830 --> 00:05:22,180
no one needs to know that my middle name is Leakey.

97
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:24,240
But there's nothing embarrassing about that.

98
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:27,630
Your father worked with Louis Leakey, a great anthropologist.

99
00:05:27,630 --> 00:05:30,380
It had nothing to do with your bed-wetting.

100
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:35,600
All m saying is that this party is the perfect opportunity for Penny

101
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:38,040
to see me as a member of her peer group,

102
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:42,650
a potential close friend,and perhaps more,

103
00:05:42,650 --> 00:05:45,730
and I don't want to look like a dork.

104
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,580
Just a heads up,fellas.

105
00:05:56,580 --> 00:06:00,500
If anyone gets lucky,I've got a dozen condoms in my quiver.

106
00:06:01,930 --> 00:06:03,750
Oh,hey,guys.

107
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:05,430
Hey. Sorry we're late.

108
00:06:05,430 --> 00:06:06,330
Late?

109
00:06:06,330 --> 00:06:07,540
It's 7:05.

110
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:09,730
And you said the party starts at 7:00.

111
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:11,860
Well,yeah,I mean,when you start a party at 7:00,

112
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:15,570
no one shows up at,you know,7:00.

113
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:18,680
It's 7:05.

114
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,390
Yes. Yes,it is.

115
00:06:20,390 --> 00:06:23,240
Okay. Well,um,come on in.

116
00:06:30,770 --> 00:06:33,630
So,what,are all the girls in the bathroom?

117
00:06:33,630 --> 00:06:36,980
Probably,but in their own homes.

118
00:06:37,470 --> 00:06:40,460
So,what time does the costume parade start?

119
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:42,290
The parade?

120
00:06:42,290 --> 00:06:45,430
Yeah,so the judges can give out the prizes for best costume.

121
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:47,320
You know,most frightening,most authentic,

122
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:51,180
most accurate visualization of a scientific principal.

123
00:06:52,790 --> 00:06:54,380
Oh,Sheldon,I'm sorry,

124
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:55,760
but there aren't going to be any parades

125
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:59,200
or judges or prizes.

126
00:06:59,770 --> 00:07:02,240
This party is just going to suck.

127
00:07:02,430 --> 00:07:04,370
No! Come on,it's going to be fun,

128
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:05,420
and you all look great.

129
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:07,030
I mean,look at you,Thor,

130
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:10,690
and,oh,Peter Pan. That's so cute.

131
00:07:10,690 --> 00:07:13,850
-Actually,Penny,he's Robin Hood. -I'm Peter Pan.

132
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:18,810
And I got a handful of pixie dust with your name on it.

133
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,890
No,you don't.

134
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,910
Uh,hey,what's Sheldon supposed to be?

135
00:07:24,910 --> 00:07:27,250
Oh,he's the Doppler effect.

136
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:30,100
Yes. It's the apparent change in the frequency of a wave

137
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:34,680
caused by relative motion between the source of the wave and the observer.

138
00:07:35,810 --> 00:07:37,580
Oh,sure,I see it now.

139
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:39,690
The Doppler effect.

140
00:07:39,690 --> 00:07:40,670
All right,I got to shower.

141
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:43,810
You guys,um,make yourselves comfortable.

142
00:07:43,810 --> 00:07:45,510
Okay.

143
00:07:46,390 --> 00:07:49,690
See? People get it.

144
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:06,230
By Odin's beard,this is good Chex mix.

145
00:08:06,230 --> 00:08:07,790
No,thanks. Peanuts.

146
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:10,910
I can't afford to swell up in these tights.

147
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:12,300
I'm confused.

148
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:15,900
If there's no costume parade,what are we doing here?

149
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:19,220
We're socializing,meeting new people.

150
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:21,820
Telepathically?

151
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:24,510
Oh,hey,when did you get here?

152
00:08:24,510 --> 00:08:25,490
Hi.

153
00:08:25,490 --> 00:08:28,380
Penny is wearing the worst Catwoman costume I've ever seen.

154
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:30,740
And that includes Halle Berry's.

155
00:08:30,740 --> 00:08:33,670
She's not Catwoman. She's just a generic cat.

156
00:08:33,670 --> 00:08:35,610
And that's the kind of sloppy costuming

157
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:39,490
which results from a lack of rules and competion.

158
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:43,690
Hey,guys,check out the sexy nurse.

159
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:49,070
I believe it's time for me to turn my head and cough.

160
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:50,990
What is your move?

161
00:08:50,990 --> 00:08:53,210
I'm going to use the mirror technique.

162
00:08:53,210 --> 00:08:55,210
She brushes her hair back,I brush my hair back...

163
00:08:55,210 --> 00:08:56,230
She shrugs,I shrug.

164
00:08:56,230 --> 00:09:00,010
Subconsciously she's thinking,"We're in sync. We belong together."

165
00:09:00,010 --> 00:09:02,430
Where do you get this stuff?

166
00:09:02,430 --> 00:09:05,370
You know,psychology journals,Internet research,

167
00:09:05,370 --> 00:09:10,100
and there's this great show on VH-1 about how to pick up girls.

168
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:14,000
Oh,if only I had his confidence.

169
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:18,020
I have such difficulty speaking to women,or around women...

170
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:22,170
or at times even effeminate men.

171
00:09:22,170 --> 00:09:23,820
If that's a working stethoscope,

172
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:27,620
maybe you'd like to hear my heart skip a beat?

173
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:28,910
No,thanks.

174
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:32,950
No,seriously,you can.I have transient idiopathic arrhythmia.

175
00:09:39,190 --> 00:09:40,830
I want to get to know Penny's friends,

176
00:09:44,710 --> 00:09:47,980
Well,I actually might be able to help.

177
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:49,060
How so?

178
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:51,550
Like Jane Goodall observing the apes,

179
00:09:51,550 --> 00:09:55,220
I initially saw their interactions as confusing and unstructured.

180
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,680
But patterns emerge.

181
00:09:56,680 --> 00:10:00,600
They have their own language,if you will.

182
00:10:00,950 --> 00:10:02,510
Go on.

183
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:06,860
Well,it seems that the newcomer approaches the existing group with the greeting,

184
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:08,760
"How wasted am I?"

185
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:12,740
Which is met with an approving chorus of "Dude."

186
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:14,680
Then what happens?

187
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:17,360
That's as far as I've gotten.

188
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,180
This is ridiculous.

189
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:20,480
I'm jumping in.

190
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,370
Good luck.

191
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:22,810
No,you're coming with me.

192
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:25,200
Oh,I hardly think so.

193
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,740
Oh,come on.

194
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:28,490
Aren't you afraid I'll embarrass you?

195
00:10:28,490 --> 00:10:31,110
Yes; but I need a wing man.

196
00:10:31,110 --> 00:10:34,050
All right,but if we're going to use flight metaphors,

197
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:39,240
I'm much more suited to being the guy from the FAA analyzing wreckage.

198
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,400
Hi.

199
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,020
Hi. Hello.

200
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:46,010
So what are you supposed to be?

201
00:10:46,010 --> 00:10:49,560
Me? I'll give you a hint.

202
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:54,350
A choo-choo train?

203
00:10:54,350 --> 00:10:56,090
Close!

204
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:01,610
A brain damaged choo-choo train?

205
00:11:02,770 --> 00:11:06,900
How wasted am I?

206
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,940
I still don't get it.

207
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:19,900
I'm the Doppler effect.

208
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,070
Okay,if that's some sort of learning disability,

209
00:11:22,070 --> 00:11:24,970
I think it's very insensitive.

210
00:11:25,890 --> 00:11:29,290
Why don't you just tell people you're a zebra?

211
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:32,500
Well,why don't you just tell people you're one of the seven dwarves?

212
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:33,720
Because I'm Frodo.

213
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:37,080
Yes,well,I'm the Doppler effect.

214
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:40,100
-Oh,no.  -What?

215
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:42,070
That's Penny's ex-boyfriend.

216
00:11:42,070 --> 00:11:44,020
What do you suppose he's doing here?

217
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:47,670
Besides disrupting the local gravity field.

218
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:51,070
If he were any bigger,he'd have moons orbiting him.

219
00:11:51,070 --> 00:11:53,800
Oh,snap.

220
00:11:54,110 --> 00:11:56,330
So,I guess we'll be leaving now.

221
00:11:56,330 --> 00:11:58,230
Why should we leave?

222
00:11:58,230 --> 00:12:03,080
For all we know he crashed the party and Penny doesn't even want him here.

223
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:06,150
You have a backup hypothesis?

224
00:12:06,150 --> 00:12:08,620
Maybe they want to be friends.

225
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:12,500
Or maybe she wants to be friends and he wants something more.

226
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,710
Then he and I are on equal ground.

227
00:12:14,710 --> 00:12:18,090
Yes,but you're much closer to it than he is.

228
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:21,780
Look,if this was 1,500 years ago,

229
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:23,700
by virtue of his size and strength,

230
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:26,250
Kurt would be entitled to his choice of female partners.

231
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:29,500
And male partners,animal partners, large primordial eggplants--

232
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:32,250
pretty much whatever tickled his fancy.

233
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:35,490
Yes,but our society has undergone a paradigm shift.

234
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:37,430
In the Information Age,Sheldon,

235
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:39,910
you and I are the alpha males.

236
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:41,720
We shouldn't have to back down.

237
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,610
True.

238
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:45,880
Why don't you text him that and see if he backs down?

239
00:12:46,470 --> 00:12:48,160
No.

240
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:52,350
I'm going to assert my dominance face-to-face.

241
00:12:52,350 --> 00:12:54,770
Face-to-face? Are you going to wait for him to sit down,

242
00:12:54,770 --> 00:12:57,560
or are you going to stand on the coffee table?

243
00:12:58,750 --> 00:12:59,860
Hello,Penny.

244
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:00,760
Hello,Kurt.

245
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:02,840
Oh,hey,guys,are you having a good time?

246
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,090
Given the reaction to my costume,

247
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:08,670
this party is a scathing indictment of the American education system.

248
00:13:08,670 --> 00:13:11,480
What,you're a zebra,right?

249
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,360
Yet another child left behind.

250
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,850
And what are you supposed to be,an elf?

251
00:13:16,850 --> 00:13:18,300
No,I'm a hobbit.

252
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:19,970
What's the difference?

253
00:13:19,970 --> 00:13:22,860
A hobbit is a mortal halfling inhabitant of Middle Earth,

254
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:26,430
whereas an elf is an immortal,tall warrior.

255
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:29,540
So why the hell would you want to be a hobbit?

256
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:31,540
Because he's neither tall nor immortal

257
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:34,170
and none of us could be The Flash.

258
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,790
Well,whatever.

259
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:37,750
Why don't you go hop off on a quest?

260
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:39,230
I'm talking to Penny here.

261
00:13:39,230 --> 00:13:41,170
I think we're all talking to Penny here.

262
00:13:41,170 --> 00:13:43,760
I'm not. No offense.

263
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,410
Okay,maybe you didn't hear me.

264
00:13:45,410 --> 00:13:47,650
-Go away.  -All right,Kurt,be nice.

265
00:13:47,650 --> 00:13:50,400
Oh,I am being nice.

266
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:52,150
Right,little buddy?

267
00:13:52,150 --> 00:13:54,370
-Kurt.  -Okay.

268
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:58,690
I understand your impulse to try to physically intimidate me.

269
00:13:58,690 --> 00:14:01,220
I mean,you can't compete with me on an intellectual level

270
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:04,190
so you're driven to animalistic puffery.

271
00:14:04,190 --> 00:14:06,690
You calling me a puffy animal?

272
00:14:06,690 --> 00:14:08,650
Of course not. No,he's not.

273
00:14:08,650 --> 00:14:10,950
You're not,right,Leonard?

274
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:13,640
No,I said "animalistic."

275
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:15,240
Of course we're all animals,

276
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:18,790
but some of us have climbed a little higher on the evolutionary tree.

277
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:21,070
If he understands that,you're in trouble.

278
00:14:21,070 --> 00:14:23,140
So,what,I'm unevolved?

279
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:25,300
You're in trouble.

280
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,680
You know,you use a lot of big words for such a little dwarf.

281
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:30,360
Okay,Kurt,please.

282
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:33,480
Penny,it's okay. I can handle this.

283
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:35,190
I am not a dwarf,

284
00:14:35,190 --> 00:14:36,860
I'm a hobbit.

285
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:38,130
A hobbit.

286
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:41,010
Are misfiring neurons in your hippocampus preventing the conversion

287
00:14:41,010 --> 00:14:44,550
from short-term to long-term memory?

288
00:14:45,990 --> 00:14:49,190
Okay,now you're starting to make me mad.

289
00:14:49,190 --> 00:14:53,420
A homo habilis discovering his opposable thumbs says what?

290
00:14:53,910 --> 00:14:55,680
What?

291
00:14:59,830 --> 00:15:01,310
I think I've made my point.

292
00:15:01,310 --> 00:15:04,720
Yeah? How about I make a point out of your pointy little head?

293
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:07,440
Let me remind you,while my moral support is absolute,

294
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:10,610
in a physical confrontation,I will be less than useless.

295
00:15:10,610 --> 00:15:12,790
There's not going to be a confrontation.

296
00:15:12,790 --> 00:15:17,090
In fact,I doubt if he can even spell "confrontation."

297
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,810
C-O-N...

298
00:15:21,810 --> 00:15:24,120
frontation!

299
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:26,080
Kurt,put him down this instant!

300
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:27,090
He started it!

301
00:15:27,090 --> 00:15:30,290
I don't care. I'm finishing it.Put him down!

302
00:15:30,290 --> 00:15:32,220
Fine.

303
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:36,250
You're one lucky little leprechaun.

304
00:15:37,330 --> 00:15:39,260
He's a hobbit!

305
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:41,590
I got your back.

306
00:15:41,910 --> 00:15:43,080
Leonard,are you okay?

307
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:45,430
Yeah,I'm fine.

308
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:49,810
It's good,it's a good party,thanks for having us.

309
00:15:49,810 --> 00:15:51,940
It's just getting a little late,so...

310
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,540
Oh,okay.

311
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:56,250
All right,well,thank you for coming.

312
00:15:58,470 --> 00:16:01,480
Happy Halloween.

313
00:16:03,550 --> 00:16:04,670
If it's any consolation,

314
00:16:04,670 --> 00:16:08,970
I thought that homo habilis line really put him in his place.

315
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:18,690
What's that?

316
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:20,460
Tea.

317
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:21,930
When people are upset,

318
00:16:21,930 --> 00:16:25,940
the cultural convention is to bring them hot beverages.

319
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:34,470
There,there.

320
00:16:36,210 --> 00:16:37,620
You want to talk about it?

321
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:39,840
-No.  -Good.

322
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:43,720
"There,there" was really all I had.

323
00:16:44,130 --> 00:16:45,230
Good night,Sheldon.

324
00:16:45,230 --> 00:16:47,280
Good night,Leonard.

325
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,690
Hey,Leonard?

326
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:55,970
Hi,Penny.

327
00:16:55,970 --> 00:16:57,930
Hey,I just wanted to make sure you were okay.

328
00:16:57,930 --> 00:17:00,500
I'm fine.

329
00:17:01,290 --> 00:17:03,890
I am so sorry about what happened.

330
00:17:03,890 --> 00:17:05,620
It's not your fault.

331
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:06,800
Yes,it is.

332
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,230
That's why I broke up with him.

333
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:11,480
He always does stuff like that.

334
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:14,770
So why was he at your party?

335
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:22,500
Well,I ran into him last week and he was just all apologetic about how he's changed.

336
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,860
And he was just going on and on and...

337
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:26,530
I believed him and I'm an idiot

338
00:17:26,530 --> 00:17:29,570
because I always believe guys like that.

339
00:17:29,570 --> 00:17:31,900
And I can't go back to my party because he's there.

340
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:33,630
And know you don't want to hear this and I'm upset

341
00:17:33,630 --> 00:17:37,320
and I'm really drunk and I just want to...

342
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:48,130
There,there.

343
00:17:50,750 --> 00:17:52,550
God,what is wrong with me?

344
00:17:52,550 --> 00:17:54,180
Nothing,you're perfect.

345
00:17:54,590 --> 00:17:55,730
I'm not perfect.

346
00:17:55,730 --> 00:17:58,120
Yes,you are.

347
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:03,470
You really think so,don't you?

348
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:17,380
Penny?

349
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:19,430
Yeah?

350
00:18:19,430 --> 00:18:22,930
How much have you had to drink tonight?

351
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:27,900
Just... a lot.

352
00:18:28,250 --> 00:18:32,390
Are you sure that your being drunk and your being angry with Kurt

353
00:18:32,390 --> 00:18:36,360
doesn't have something to do with what's going on here?

354
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:39,780
It might.

355
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:42,860
Boy,you're really smart.

356
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:46,540
Yeah,I'm a frickin' genius.

357
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:52,170
Leonard,you are so great.

358
00:18:52,170 --> 00:18:55,110
Why can't all guys be like you?

359
00:18:55,110 --> 00:18:56,690
Because if all guys were like me,

360
00:18:56,690 --> 00:19:00,320
the human race couldn't survive.

361
00:19:03,430 --> 00:19:05,210
I should probably go.

362
00:19:05,210 --> 00:19:07,840
Probably.

363
00:19:15,650 --> 00:19:18,140
Thank you.

364
00:19:27,490 --> 00:19:30,880
That's right,you saw what you saw.

365
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:35,570
That's how we roll in the Shire.

366
00:19:42,810 --> 00:19:44,780
Coming.

367
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:51,900
Hey,have you seen Koothrappali?

368
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,640
He's not here.

369
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:57,290
Maybe the Avengers summoned him.

370
00:19:57,290 --> 00:20:00,530
He's not the Marvel Comics Thor,he's the original Norse god.

371
00:20:00,530 --> 00:20:03,010
Thank you for the clarification.

372
00:20:03,010 --> 00:20:04,300
I'm supposed to give him a ride home.

373
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,900
Well,I'm sure he'll be fine.

374
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:09,300
He has his hammer.

375
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:19,670
I have to say,you are an amazing man.

376
00:20:19,670 --> 00:20:23,210
You're gentle,and passionate.

377
00:20:23,210 --> 00:20:28,110
And,my God,you are such a good listener.

